WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.487
Python can assign several values in one line.

00:00:03.487 --> 00:00:11.877
Here, Jordan goes into employee_name, thirty goes into age, and fifty thousand goes into salary.

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:19.595
The order matters. The first value is matched with the first variable, the second with the second, and so on.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:26.254
This feature is convenient when the values clearly belong together, but readability still matters.

00:00:26.254 --> 00:00:31.959
If one line becomes crowded or confusing, separate assignments are perfectly fine.

00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:39.733
Run the example, then replace the fictional values with another set and confirm that each variable receives the correct

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:40.380
value.
